================================================================================
COMPONENT & THIRD-PARTY LICENSING DETAILS
================================================================================

Historical ASSDraw source files which carry ai-chan's or the Aegisub Project's
original notice remain under those respective notices. This file serves as the
primary license for the repository and binary distributions; it does not alter
the license of any third-party component.

1. Project Maintenance & Fork Contributions (BSD 3-Clause)
   - Original ASSDraw3 implementation by ai-chan (2007) and subsequent
     maintenance by the Aegisub Project (2008-2012).
   - Application modernization, CMake/installer pipeline, DPI handling, bitmap
     bundles, i18n automation, and active maintenance (2025-present) by
     Kerim Demirkaynak.
   - Selected patches and features integrated from sibling forks (including
     MIRIMIRIM, amanosatosi, and biki-desu) remain under the BSD 3-Clause
     License; see README.md and NOTICE.md for contributor credits.

2. Anti-Grain Geometry (AGG) Spline Code
   - Historical GPL-marked custom spline sources found in certain reference
     forks are explicitly excluded from this repository.
   - This project uses the pinned external AGG 2.6 spline code under its
     permissive non-copyleft notice (see NOTICE.md).

3. GUI Toolkit & Standard Translations (wxWindows Library Licence)
   - Native builds link statically against wxWidgets 3.3.4, distributed under
     the wxWindows Library Licence (installed under licenses/).
   - Standard widget translations in vendor/wxlocale originate from wxWidgets
     v3.3.1 and retain their original contributor notices, wxWindows license,
     and LGPL texts, separate from the application catalogs in po/.
   - This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

4. Documentation & Bundled Assets
   - docs/help/original is an offline-adapted HTML export of ai-chan's original
     docs/ASSDraw3.chm manual, retaining all original text, illustrations, and
     author credits.
   - Toolbar icons are adapted from Font Awesome Free 7.2.0 (Copyright 2026
     Fonticons, Inc., https://fontawesome.com), licensed under CC BY 4.0
     (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Original SVG files and
     license text are retained in vendor/fontawesome.

For exact commit hashes, file manifests, and dependency details, see NOTICE.md,
README.md, and the licenses/ directory.
